   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to enrollment eligibility for\ncertain persons in the address confidentiality program",
    "basePrintNo": "S7664",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7664-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §108, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7664\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to enrollment eligibility\nfor certain persons in the address confidentiality program\n\n \n PURPOSE::\n\nRelates to enrollment eligibility for certain persons in the address\nconfidentiality program\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS::\n\nSection 1 titles the bill \"address confidentiality for child survivors\nand their families act\"\n\nSection 2 provides that victims of child abduction are eligible to\nparticipate in the address confidentiality program run by the office of\nthe secretary of state.\n\nSection 3 provides the effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION::\n\nCurrently, victims of child abduction do not have statutory access to\nNew York State's Address Confidentiality Program (ACP). The ACP allows\nsurvivors of certain crimes the ability to protect their addresses from\npublic records so that their abusers cannot use public resources to\nlocate survivors. This legislation seeks to include victims of child\nabduction as eligible participants to the Address Confidentiality\nProgram, empowering the victims and allowing them to rebuild their lives\nwith privacy.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY::\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS::\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE::\n\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
