    "lawCode": "Amd §108, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7664A\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to enrollment eligibility\nfor certain persons in the address confidentiality program\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nRelates to enrollment eligibility for certain persons in the address\nconfidentiality program\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 titles the bill \"address confidentiality for victims of\nkidnapping\"\n\nSection 2 provides that victims of kidnapping are eligible to partic-\nipate in the address confidentiality program run by the office of the\nsecretary of state.\n\nSection 3 provides the effective date.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION:\n\nAmends \"victims of child abduction\" to \"victims of kidnapping.\"\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently, victims of kidnapping do not have statutory access to New\nYork State's Address Confidentiality Program (ACP). The ACP allows\nsurvivors of certain crimes the ability to protect their addresses from\npublic records so that their abusers cannot use public resources to\nlocate survivors. This legislation seeks to include victims of kidnap-\nping as eligible participants to the Address Confidentiality Program,\nempowering the victims and allowing them to rebuild their lives with\nprivacy.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
